{{senderName}}
{{senderTitle}}, {{organizationName}}

Hi {{contactName}},

Thank you for taking the time to connect — I've been thinking about our conversation, and I wanted to put something more concrete on paper.

{{organizationName}} is building AI literacy programs for rural South Carolina communities — people who are already feeling the effects of an AI-driven economy but have had very little access to education, training, or tools to navigate it. Our approach is grounded in where people actually are: practical, jargon-free, and built around real work and real lives.

I believe a partnership with {{contactOrganization}} could be genuinely powerful for both of us. Here's why:

{{partnershipBenefits}}

What I'm specifically hoping to explore:

{{specificAsk}}

I want to be direct: I'm not asking for money. I'm asking for a relationship. The organizations I most want to partner with are the ones already doing good work in these communities — like {{contactOrganization}}. A formal partnership could mean something as simple as co-hosting an event, sharing each other's networks, or building a program together. Whatever makes sense for where you are.

I've attached a one-page overview of {{organizationName}} for context. I'd welcome any questions, pushback, or ideas you have — and I'm happy to revise this based on what would actually be useful to {{contactOrganization}}.

Thank you for considering this.

With appreciation,
{{senderName}}
{{senderTitle}}, {{organizationName}}
